  "copyStatus": "Copied.",
  "copiedText": "Mode Fluency self-diagnostic\nDefault stance: Oracle (Truth to a hard question)\nLoad-bearing layer: Judgment (What to doubt while doing)\nCharacteristic failure: Confident plausible prose taken as fact\nGuardrail to adopt: Ask for the uncertainty before the answer. Treat the answer as a claim, not a verdict.\nAutonomy mode: Directed: you describe, AI types, you review. Spec rigor required: Medium.\nAmbition: Altitude: Going up in abstraction and considering the outcome rather than the individual task. Ask: “what do you want to happen next? What's the goal beyond the goal?” (Felix Rieseberg)\nWatch next: AI 301 @ Workplace (https://youtu.be/R2p5aFcb0lY). Failure patterns and the eval mindset: how to know an output is wrong before it costs you.\nNote: You re-entered at the Context layer. For the Oracle, check Judgment first.\nNote: That is step 1 of 5 on the checking ladder, the weakest: in a long thread, it will tell you that you're absolutely right. Move at least to a fresh chat.\nFrom the Mode Fluency prototype (Henrique Jr. Sanchez). Framework sources: https://github.com/hjasanchez/agentic-engineering",
